 heat uh that one year a few years  many years ago now i guess and  and you know things kept going and  players  yeah were more conscious of hydrating  but they they  moved on with the game it's sort of like  nascar when  when they have a death they just keep  going and it's amazing to me but  as you said rudy gobert shut down things  instantly when he tested positive and  who knows where we would be or how long  we would have gone if that hadn't  happened but it seems likely that  we would have had more positive cases  pretty quickly after that but that shut  down everything and  all it's going to take probably is one  death especially a death of a player  that we're going to see this whole i  keep calling it a house of cards because  i do think it's a house of cards we have  going here right now  well and part of the reason is  the way that we have handled the  pandemic as  a society you know people will say well  hey the bundesliga soccer league they  were able to finish  their season premier league finished  their season they're starting up another  one on september 12.  yeah in their countries it's been  contained  in their countries it's been controlled  what's happening here  is we're trying to play football in  these communities where  the virus is just rampant and the  schools are going to open in a lot of  these communities or at least they're  going to try to open them  and and this idea of sending everyone  home  at night even if everyone goes home and  stays home and doesn't go out and do any  of the things that could get them in  trouble with their teams or with the  league  you have other people that you may be  living with who are out about doing  things  and with the prevalence of the virus it  makes it impossible  to keep it away from the players the  coaches the people who go home at night  that's why we're seeing  teams set up these unofficial voluntary  bubbles like the saints in training camp  like the buccaneers are going to have  available getting a hotel  basically booking it for the entire  season and having it available for  anybody who wants to be there  and the more guys who are there shireen  the more pressure there's going to be on  the guys who go home  to not go home and that may be the only  chance look i  there are people in the league who  believe they could have pulled off a  full bubble if they really wanted to do  it if they had started planning it back  in march when they should have  not in july or august when they say oh  crap maybe we should have a full bubble  it's a little late now to do that  but the city by city bubble may be the  only way to pull this  off whether it's voluntary whether at  some point the union agrees to it  but this is something that coaches  players staff need to be thinking of  there may be a full lockdown where  you're in the same city as your family  but you're not going to see them  until the end of the season and that  that's another occasion to have an  opt-out window  even if it's a limited one because there  may be guys then who say sorry i'm just  not going to do this this isn't what i  signed up for but that may be the only  way to pull this off shereen and that  may be the only way to keep  someone from ultimately getting it and  dying  yeah we saw it with andrew whitworth is  the perfect example of that  his nanny went out to lunch with the  family friend ate lunch came home  gave it to everyone in the family  everyone in his family they passed it on  to his in-laws  his father-in-law ended up in the  hospital and nearly died from this  so it shows you how this thing can  spread and kids are going back to school  and they are going to bring it home  and families are going to get it so the  best way to do it obviously is to  sequester the player and  some players are going to do it and some  aren't and it is going to put pressure  on those players  who don't do it because they are going  to be obviously way  way way more subjected to the virus  chances of contracting the virus than  than guys who are staying in a hotel  around the team  yeah i think creativity flexibility  commitment to doing what needs to be  done to protect the players and to get  the games in  everyone now has a clear financial  incentive to get every game  in because the players are only going to  get paid for the games  that are played and if you have a  guaranteed salary it really isn't  guaranteed we've got the stories at pft  check it out and if nothing else at this  point because you can't opt out it  doesn't matter  but the guys with fully guaranteed  salaries have extra incentive  to ensure that their players make good  decisions  and maybe to influence them to volunteer  to stay at the hotel and draw that  bubble around  each team in the hopes of getting all  256 games in  all right the man who quoted the man who  said the only thing we have to fear  is fear itself met with the media  yesterday tom brady had some things to  say you'll hear  about it next here on pro football talk  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights  from nbc sports
 

